It does NOT implement `Drop`. So dropping a `HANDLE` value without calling `CloseHandle` leaks the handle.

Also, `HANDLE::default()` returns `HANDLE(0)` which is a null handle. So `if !self.job.0.is_null()` checks whether it's valid. After `std::mem::take()`, the handle becomes `HANDLE(0)`. So the take_stdout_handle / take_stderr_handle pattern works correctly.

